#: commerce_currencies.module:19
msgid "After installation"
msgstr ""

#: commerce_currencies.module:20
msgid "Upon installation, existing commerce entities (product types, variations, etc) were scanned and the original, single-currency <kbd>commerce_price</kbd> fields got replaced with new, multi-currency variants. Widgets (single or list price) and display settings were also modified. Previously existing prices were migrated to the new setup. In a stock Commerce store, this already means fully functional multi-currency operation, you don't need any other change."
msgstr ""

#: commerce_currencies.module:21
msgid "If you use custom entities, either created in the UI or from code, make sure you replace old <kbd>commerce_price</kbd> fields with the new <kbd>commerce_currencies_price</kbd> type. They appear in the usual field UI among the Commerce related field types as <em>Price (multi-currency)</em>."
msgstr ""

#: commerce_currencies.module:22
msgid "Also take care of custom theme templates referencing the old <kbd>price</kbd> and <kbd>list_price</kbd> fields, the new, automatically created ones have the names <kbd>commerce_currencies_price</kbd> and <kbd>commerce_currencies_list_price</kbd>."
msgstr ""

